1. Tokenizer
----------------------------------------------------------------------
The tokenizer shipped with molecule is derived from the Qwen2.5 tokenizer
(Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B), originally released by Alibaba Cloud / Qwen team under
the Apache License 2.0.

  - We reuse the Qwen2.5 tokenization scheme (vocabulary pieces, byte-level
    fallback, special tokens, ChatML template) and then reduce the vocabulary
    to 32K by corpus-frequency pruning. The model weights are fully
    self-developed and not derived from Qwen2.5.

  - Qwen2.5: https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen2.5
    License: Apache-2.0

----------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Fused architecture mechanisms (学习/融合来源，非整框架)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
molecule is a general decoder-only Transformer that selectively fuses
individual open-source attention / normalization / training techniques
rather than adopting any whole framework. Sources of inspiration include:

  - RoPE (Rotary Position Embedding) + NTK-aware scaling
      Su et al., "RoFormer" (2021); NTK-aware interpolation by bloc97 (2023).
      Adopted from Llama / Mistral / Qwen / DeepSeek / Gemma conventions.

  - GQA (Grouped-Query Attention)
      Ainslie et al., "GQA: Training Generalized Multi-Query Transformer
      Models from Multi-Head Checkpoints" (2023). Used by Llama-2/3, Qwen,
      Gemma, MobileLLM.

  - SwiGLU activation
      Shazeer, "GLU Variants Improve Transformer" (2020); used by Llama /
      Gemma / Qwen / DeepSeek. Intermediate size set to 8/3 * hidden.

  - RMSNorm + Pre-Norm
      Zhang & Sennrich, "Root Mean Square Layer Normalization" (2019);
      standard in the Llama / Qwen / Gemma families.

  - QK-Norm (normalizing Q/K before RoPE)
      OLMo 2 (AllenAI), Gemma 3, MiniMax-M2 conventions.

  - Logit soft-capping (attention 50.0 / final 30.0)
      Gemma 2 (Gemmateam, 2024).

  - DeepNorm (residual / attention gain scaling for deep narrow stacks)
      Wang et al., "DeepNet: Scaling Transformers to 1,000 Layers" (2022);
      used by DeepSeek.

  - MTP (Multi-Token Prediction, 1 module, shared embed + output head)
      DeepSeek-AI, "DeepSeek-V3 Technical Report" (2024).

  - Tied embeddings (input = output embedding)
      MobileLLM (Liu et al., 2024, Meta); PanGu-π conventions.

  - Muon optimizer (orthogonalization of 2D weights via Newton-Schulz)
      Jordan et al., "Muon: An optimizer for hidden layers" (2024).

  - WSD (Warmup-Stable-Decay) schedule
      Hu et al., "MiniCPM: Unveiling the Potential of Small Language Models"
      (2024, ICLR).

Each of the above techniques is a published, permissively-documented method.
No source code from those projects is copied verbatim into molecule; the
implementation is written independently by codecloud-dev.

